    description: "Found by the 2026-10-25 docstring staleness audit (dev 95c0ff7b93): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier confirmed it by reading the code itself (a repro where stated). Severity is not asserted; impact not measured on the corpus.\n\n- fish.py: `--argument-names` and `-a` are not captured -- evidence: repro output `SYM fish:a.fish:1-3:f:function function f ()`, `SYM fish:a.fish:4-6:g:function function g ()`, `SYM fish:a.fish:7-9:h:function function h (p, q)`.\n\nNot asserted: that the fix is the one sketched above, or that no other language has the same shape."  # e79c
